I look at the vegetable shopkeeper.
There is a small basket there.
There is a green vegetable in that basket.
It is long.
I do not know this vegetable.
I point my finger at it.
"What is this?" I ask him.
"That is bitter gourd," the shopkeeper says.
"Do you want bitter gourd?" he asks.
I like new vegetables.
"Yes, I want one," I say.
"I want exactly one bitter gourd," I say again.
The shopkeeper takes one bitter gourd.
He smiles.
"It is bitter," he says.
I smile back.
I like bitter food too.
He puts it in my bag.
